{
  "about": "FIPS 10-4 country codes, which GDELT uses for ActionGeo_CountryCode, with their ISO 3166-1 alpha-3 codes and English short names: every row of countrycode's code list that has both codes, sorted by FIPS code. Read by volatility/scripts/gvi.mjs, which leaves out Antarctica and the French Southern Territories, names WE (the West Bank, with the Gaza Strip's GZ) Palestine, and adds the codes GDELT uses that the list does not map: KV (Kosovo), OD (South Sudan) and RB (Belgrade, counted with Serbia). Extracted once, so no build fetches it; to refresh it, extract the same three columns from a newer commit and record that commit and the file's sha256 here.",
